    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485-a2">

                <pb facs="0775" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg647"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    16.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. du Bocage to Mr. Lewis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 30,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In answer to the notes which your excellency was plesased to address me on
                    February 16 and June 24 ultimo, I have the honor to say that no laws exist in
                    the province of Mozambique forbidding foreign missionaries giving the indigenous
                    population the instruction they need, and developing among them love for work
                    and virtue, thus leading them on the road of progress and civilization.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. V. BARBOZA DU BOCAGE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
